summary.value:
Reviewers agree the idea is novel and potentially broadly useful, with a strong positive review emphasizing convincing cross-domain demonstrations (proteins, images, materials). The main concerns raised across reviews are: 
- sensitivity to the choice of embedding and similarity kernel and how practitioners should choose these; 
- hyperparameter choices (notably the Vendi order q, and kernel / kNN settings) and stability of rankings; 
- clarity around approximation and reproducibility of the ranking; 
- presentation and experimental choices (one review also contained multiple factual misunderstandings, limiting its usefulness).
